{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"Rule 6c-11 requires **written basket policies and procedures** covering basket construction and acceptance, including detailed parameters for **custom baskets**, and a process for revisions or deviations. The policies must set out revisions to the basket, if any, and specify the titles or roles of adviser employees authorized to review each custom basket for compliance; the adviser must maintain records of that review.\n\nA **custom basket** is a basket that is (1) non-representative of the ETF’s portfolio or differs from the initial basket used that business day, or (2) a representative basket that is non-pro-rata or differs from that initial basket. “Non-standard order” is an operational/exchange or AP term—not a Rule 6c-11 category—and does not by itself make a basket custom.\n\nKeep basket policies, exchanged basket contents, AP identities, cash balancing amounts, and custom-basket compliance records for **five years**, with the first two readily accessible. (17 C.F.R. § 270.6c-11(c)(3), (d)(2).)"}}
